## **5. Regression tests that should be added immediately**

The existing test suites are extensive, but several high-risk integration paths are missing.

| Test                        | Input / scenario                                              | Required behavior                                            |
| --------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |
| Account isolation           | Sign in as A, cache a review, sign out, sign in as B          | B cannot view, edit, delete or sync A's review               |
| Anonymous adoption          | Sign in after creating local-only reports                     | Reports remain local until explicitly adopted for cloud sync |
| Session-switch race         | Start review as A and switch to B during inference            | Result cannot be saved to B                                  |
| Provider fail-closed        | Select custom provider, then make key unavailable             | No request is sent to Firebase                               |
| Oversized ledger round-trip | Serialize and reload a 100 KB structured findings ledger      | Every finding and anchor survives intact                     |
| Legacy cloud document       | Load a document without validation fields                     | Status remains `LEGACY_UNVALIDATED`                          |
| Entailment polarity         | “Treatment did not reduce mortality”                          | Must not support the opposite allegation                     |
| GRADE missing evidence      | Review with incomplete outcome data                           | No unsupported high-certainty rating                         |
| Scanned paper               | 10-page image-only PDF with five page images                  | Full-document appraisal is blocked or explicitly limited     |
| Statistical saturation      | Paper with 100+ quantitative claims                           | No silent first-match omission                               |
| Actual PDF rendering        | Very long titles, tables, rationales and multilingual symbols | Finished PDF contains all expected text without clipping     |
| Concurrent edits            | Update bookmark and notes nearly simultaneously               | Both changes persist                                         |

The benchmark should also include **the full original psychiatric-bed article**, rather than relying only on synthetic excerpts reproducing its known numerical inconsistency.

## **6. A practical engineering repair plan**

**Release blocker A — Account and provider isolation**

Owner-scoped Room data, explicit anonymous-data adoption, session-bound tasks and fail-closed provider routing.

*Done when:* No review, chat, API credential or upload can cross account boundaries.

**Release blocker B — Lossless persistence**

Remove JSON truncation, add versioning and checksums, protect local originals and implement atomic synchronization.

*Done when:* Cloud round-trips reproduce the complete local scientific report.

**Release blocker C — Scientific truth preservation**

Replace lexical entailment with context-aware verification; allow only adjudicated findings to influence scores and authoritative prose.

*Done when:* Every consequential statement is traceable to scientifically appropriate evidence.

**Quality upgrade D — Clinical and statistical validity**

Build genuinely outcome-specific certainty assessments, preserve interval types and eliminate claim-extraction saturation.

*Done when:* Methodologically valid alternative interpretations are not mislabeled as errors.

**Quality upgrade E — Publication-grade reporting**

Independently validate exported PDF bytes, add navigable source evidence and establish real-manuscript benchmarks.

*Done when:* Expert review and automated visual checks both approve the generated reports.

## **7. Final audit judgment**

The latest version is considerably more capable than the earlier builds. Its numerical reconstruction, quote anchoring, epistemic safeguards and tests show real engineering progress.

But I would **not yet classify it as release-ready for confidential manuscript evaluation**.

The most urgent defects are the cross-account data paths, silent provider substitution and loss-prone cloud serialization. The most urgent scientific defects are lexical entailment being used as confirmation, and unverified detector outputs or AI-generated prose potentially influencing authoritative conclusions.

For the next engineering iteration, I recommend **fixing these integrity and isolation failures before adding any more reviewer personas, statistical detectors or report sections**.

**Verification scope:** This is a source-level audit of commit `cae0a7d`. I inspected the GitHub repository, but did not execute the Android app, run Gradle, reproduce the account-switch sequence on devices, or complete live-model evaluations. The documented code paths are grounded in the current source; runtime behavior and fixes should be confirmed by the regression tests above.